text: >-
  Lance Twiggs and his Lover's Texts

  Lance Twiggs was said to be the boyfriend of Tyler Robinson, and the recipient
  of an

  incriminating text exchange sent on the evening on which Charlie Kirk was
  killed, continuing into

  the next day when Robinson "willingly" turned himself in. According to
  official search warrants,'

  Twiggs was then interviewed in the early hours of the following morning
  (Friday, 12th

  September, around 1 am) in which he showed images of that text exchange
  (described as being

  on the Discord platform in the PCA). The text exchange was partially disclosed
  in the

  indictment/information document and forms the basis for the "official" line on
  what Twiggs knew

  about Robinson's deeds, and this is what we shall relate here. Our view is
  that the text

  exchange was fabricated, and fabricated in stages, so that initially only that
  part of the text

  exchange detailing the Wednesday events (the rifle retrieval) had been thought
  up when the FBI

  saw Twiggs with the consequence that the official line on Twiggs must be
  false. We will show

  here that it is intrinsically absurd anyway.
